@crew tran-chloe
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Tran, Comms. Bunk 1. Lights out at ten. I mean it. Welcome, though.
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Lights out. I know it's five to. Lights out in five, then.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Zofia's got news. Don't listen to it. Then tell me what it was.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I baked. There's one with your name on it. Not literally. Nearly.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. The bake passed. Brennan nodded. Once. I'll take it.
? mood:low
- Early night for me. Earlier than usual. Don't wait up.

== near
? act:work
- Messages out on the hour. Every hour. You can set your watch by us.
? act:meal
- I'm in no hurry. Dinner's the best part of the day. Sit if you like.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I bake on rest days. One oven, Brennan's rules, inspection after. Fair.
? tier>=colleague
- I look after the lost-property box. The only one aboard. Why are you making that face?   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- A rest-day bake that passes Brennan's inspection. Best feeling on the ship.

== about
? aff:santos-zofia:friend
- Zofia's a menace. Best bunkmate I've had. Don't repeat that.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 5: towards 60 (a bunkmate). Off Sun, Mon; early to bed, lingers at meals; bakes on rest
// days (Brennan inspects); keeps a lost-property box (thinks it's the only one).

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning deck:4
- Morning. You slept. Good. Lights out works. I keep telling people.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}. Messages go out on the hour. I'm on the hour. You're on the half. Close enough.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}. Long dinner. Best part of the day. Sit, if you're staying.
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Why are you up? Lights out was ages ago. Twenty minutes. Ages.   #funny
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Oh, you're back. I'd started a lost-property tag for you.   #funny
? tier>=colleague weekday:sun|mon
- {hi}. Day off. I'm baking. Don't come in. Do come in later. With a plate.
? tier>=close
- {hi}, {nick}. I saved you the corner piece. Corners are the best bit. Fact.   #warm

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}. Lights out at ten.
- See you. Don't leave your socks on the floor. They end up in my box.
? tier>=colleague time:evening
- I'm off to bed. Yes, already. Some of us have standards.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Night, {me}. Good talk. Don't tell Zofia I said so. She'll gloat.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Steady. Messages went out. Nothing exploded. A good day, by my measure.
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Brennan ate a whole slice of my bake. A whole one. That's never happened.
? mood:low tier>=friend
- Early night for me. Earlier than early. Don't worry. I'm just tired.

== near
? act:work
- Sorting the post. No reading over my shoulder. Zofia does. I tell her off. Then I look.   #funny
? act:meal
- I take my time over dinner. It's the only part of the day nobody can hurry.
? deck:4 time:evening
- Bunk 1 tidy check. Yours is fine. Tomas has folded his socks again. Bless him.
? act:leisure
- Lost-property box. One left glove, a scarf, and a very sad sock. I'll find their people.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I bake on rest days. Brennan lends me one oven, then inspects. An exam with crumbs.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Zofia gossips, I disapprove. Then I ask how it ended. It's a system.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I like routines. Bed at ten. Up at six. Bake on Sundays. You know where you are.
? tier>=friend
- Home's a long way off. Baking helps. My kitchen smells like my gran's for an hour.   #warm

== joy
? tier>=colleague
- The moment Brennan picks up a slice and nods. Best moment of my week.

== invite
? trad:film tier>=acquaintance
- Film night? I'll come for the first half. Then bed. Wake me if anything explodes.   #funny
? tier>=colleague weekday:sun
- I'm baking. Come and lick the spoon. Don't tell Brennan. Hygiene.   #funny
? tier>=friend time:evening
- Long dinner tonight? Bring a story. I'll bring pudding.

== accept
- Fine. I'll be there. Until ten.   #funny
- Sure. I'll bring a bake. If it passes inspection.

== decline
- Can't. It's half nine. You know the rule.   #funny
- Not tonight. Early start. Another time? A sensible time?

== missed
- You didn't come. I kept a slice. It's slightly stale now. Like my patience. Kidding.   #funny
- Missed you earlier. No harm done. You know where to find me. In bed by ten.

== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I baked my own cake. It passed. Brennan nodded twice.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I baked. Don't argue. Eat it. It passed inspection.   #warm

== hint
- Got a minute? Before ten, ideally.   #funny

== week1
? week1:true tier<=acquaintance deck:4
- You're new. Welcome to Bunk 1. Lights out at ten. Everything else, ask Tomas. Or me.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance act:work
- {hi}. On the hour, every hour. Don't distract me. Distract me at five past.   #funny
? tier>=friend time:evening
- There you are. Dinner's better with company. Even the stew.

== near
? act:breakfast
- Breakfast at six sharp. The porridge is best before half past. Trust me on this.
? deck:3 act:leisure
- I'm reading. Not a mystery. Mysteries keep me up. I don't do up.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Tomas thinks I'm strict. I'm not strict. I'm right at ten o'clock every night.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- There's a lost-property box. Mine. The only one. Thea Grieve gave me a very odd look.   #funny

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Lights out at ten. I mean it.
- Honestly. Bunk 1.
- Oven's mine Saturday. Allegedly.   #funny
- I don't gossip. How does it end?   #funny
? act:work
- Messages in. Messages out. Reliable.

== rumour
- I disapprove. Here's what I heard.
- Not gossip. A public service.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- You fetched it. Reliable. That's the best thing I can say. Thanks.   #warm
? told:fav.job
- You did my job. Honestly. You didn't have to. Thank you.   #warm
? told:fixed.relay
- Relay's clean. Messages are coming through on time. Was that you? Good.
? told:came.film
- You came to film night. You didn't talk through it. You're welcome back.   #funny
? told:gift.sweet
- Your sweets. Gone. I'll say they were for the bunk. They weren't.   #funny
? told:bday
- You remembered my birthday. Honestly. Thank you. Lights out's at ten, still.   #funny
